{"name":"Skipping Stone","hex":"#d0cbb6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"skipping","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of skip"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act by which something is skipped or omitted.","The game, activity, or exercise of jump rope."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skipping"},{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alexz Johnson","blocks":[{"text":"Alexzandra Spencer Johnson is a Canadian actress, singer, songwriter, and musician. Known for her distinctive sound since her debut in 2010, her first album, Voodoo, was independently released with her brother, Brendan Johnson. Over the years, she has released several albums and EPs, including: The Basement Recordings series (2011–2013), Skipping Stone (2012) and her sophomore album Let 'Em Eat Cake (2014). She continued to evolve with subsequent albums A Stranger Time (2017), Still Alive (2020) and Seasons (2023)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Alexz_Johnson_2015_%28Crop%29.jpg/330px-Alexz_Johnson_2015_%28Crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexz_Johnson"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of 